HST Office: the File tab (backstage) in the HST frame coat — tests and interface only (red build).


With the coat on (FrameCoat/Backstage under UiCoat/Enabled or HST_UI_COAT, never in high contrast) every colour
of the File panel and its title band comes from the design tokens (<vcl/hst/designtokens.hxx>), and the left
column is the Start Center's: the side panel colour, a token pill (DrawPill) for the selected and the hovered
item, the keyboard focus ring (DrawFocusRing) on the focused item's pill, the navigation type (type::Nav,
NavSelected) and 40 px items 4 px apart, lowered only when the panel is too short for them (down to 24 px or the
text's height). Page titles and the greeting take type::Title, section headings type::Strong. The blocks of the
pages (the Home tiles, the document's properties, the export choices) are cards: the card fill on the frame
surface, 12 px inside; on GTK also the card's corners and border (vcl/source/hst/coat/css/backstage.cxx). The
title band's back button is a round DrawRoundRect in the coat. Behaviour, commands, ids, accessible names and the
keyboard order are unchanged.

- sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstagecoat.{hxx,cxx} (new): the panel's colours in each look (GetBackstageColors),
  the coat's item painting and sizes, the tile page preview; hstbackstagelegacycolors.hxx (new) holds the earlier
  look's colours, the only colour literals of the panel's code. FrameCoat/Backstage=false (or the coat off)
  restores the earlier look exactly.
- sfx2/uiconfig/ui/hstbackstage.ui: the left column's items are 4 px apart (spacing, no item touching another);
  style classes hst-backstage-nav and hst-backstage-card for the GTK CSS; the three card blocks get 12 px inside.
- The Print page fits the panel through the File panel's placement (hst-backstage-panel-beside-banner.patch);
  a narrower panel shrinks the print preview first (the page's boxes give way), no scrolled container.
- CppunitTest_sfx2_hst_backstagecoat: token colours light/dark, the earlier look's colours, the pill and the
  focus ring at 100/125 %, the item height fitting the panel, no colour literal in the panel's code, no coat in
  high contrast.

License: these upstream-derived files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the CSS fragment is
LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary like the coat's other files.

